@startuml hil_roundtrip_sequence
title K9-AIF HIL Round Trip — RequiresHIL → BaseHILOrchestrator → Router

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 160

actor "UI / Caller" as UI
participant "K9EventRouter" as Router
participant "Orchestrator\n(SBB, e.g. FraudOrchestrator)" as Orch
participant "Squad" as Squad
participant "Agent" as Agent
participant "BaseHILOrchestrator" as HILOrch
participant "RoutingStateStore\n(hil_pending table)" as Store
queue "Kafka\nhil.requests.<queue>" as ReqTopic
queue "Kafka\nhil.replies.<queue>" as ReplyTopic
actor "Human reviewer\n(e.g. k9x-hil)" as Human

== Forward flow — one Kafka hop, then plain calls ==
UI -> Router: event (fraud_alert)
Router -> Router: route() — event_type -> domain topic
Router -> Orch: (domain topic consumed) execute_flow(payload)
Orch -> Squad: execute(payload)
Squad -> Agent: execute(step_context)

== Trigger — Agent/Squad may raise, never publish ==
Agent -> Agent: fraud_probability > threshold
Agent -->> Squad: raise RequiresHIL(reason, context, priority)
note right of Agent
  Deliberate exception, not a return flag —
  guarantees propagation through a Squad's
  sequential flow even if the Squad author
  never checks for it. Agent/Squad still
  never touch Kafka directly (see CLAUDE.md
  Kafka-ownership carve-out).
end note
Squad -->> Orch: RequiresHIL propagates\n(logged, re-raised — not caught)

== Catch + halt — only the Orchestrator touches Kafka ==
Orch -> Orch: except RequiresHIL as exc:
Orch -> HILOrch: handle_requires_hil(exc, payload)\n(real Orchestrator-to-Orchestrator call —\nsecond deliberate rule carve-out)
HILOrch -> HILOrch: generate correlation_id
HILOrch -> Store: record_hil_pending(correlation_id,\n  resume_module, resume_class, reply_to, payload)
HILOrch -> ReqTopic: publish_to(hil.requests.<queue>, message)
HILOrch -->> Orch: {status: pending_hil, correlation_id, reply_to}
Orch -->> UI: {status: pending_hil, "check back later"}
note over Orch, UI
  Never blocks waiting for a decision —
  a HIL review can take hours or days.
end note

== Time passes — human reviews, out of band ==
ReqTopic -> Human: HIL request
Human -> ReplyTopic: decision (approve / reject / escalate)

== Resume — Router listens across every hil.replies.* topic ==
ReplyTopic -> Router: (pattern-subscribed via\nmessage_bus.subscribe_async(pattern="hil\\.replies\\..*"))
Router -> Store: get_hil_pending(correlation_id)
Store -->> Router: pending row (resume payload)
Router -> Router: resumed_payload = {**pending.payload,\n  hil_decision: message}
Router -> Router: route(resumed_payload)\n(reuse — resuming IS re-routing,\nnot a second mechanism)
Router -> Orch: (domain topic) execute_flow(resumed_payload)
Router -> Store: resolve_hil_pending(correlation_id)

@enduml
